duate Majors And Minors Graduate Studies Workforce Development Schools & Programs Connected Learning Academic Catalog & Calendar Academic Centers Academic Support Lasell Insights Study Abroad Registrar Campus Life Activities & Involvement Housing & Residential Life Health and Wellness Dining Student Support Career Center Online Bookstore & Gear Shop Connected Start Fall Move-in and Orientation Athletics LaserPride - Official site of Lasell Athletics Varsity Sports Recruits Lasers & Boomer Athletic Facilities Recreation and Intramurals Alumni Alumni News Alumni Events Ways to Give Leaves Graduate Studies Find Your Program Academics Tuition & Aid Admissions Lasell Approach Parents & Families myLasell Interactive Map Search Submit search Center for Career Readiness & Internship Programs Home › Campus Life › Career Center Get Career Ready at Lasell As a Lasell student, you'll start preparing for your future career on day one. Our career advisors, faculty, academic advisors, and others work with you to identify academic majors and interests, explore career options, gain work experience, and develop the professional skills and career readiness competencies employers are seeking — all while you’re at Lasell. 1. Get Started Use your Career Ready Roadmap to take part in important career-related activities throughout all 4 years. Career Ready Roadmap >> 2. Gain Professional Experience Build valuable professional skills and experience through internships, micro-work projects, and on-campus jobs. Find Internships & Jobs >> 3. Explore Career Resources Get resources to identify your major, research career paths, write a stand-out resume, ace the interview, and more. Career Resources >> Upcoming Career Events​ See all events >> Lasell University's education program has been recognized by Colleges of Distinction for its excellence. Lasell actively prepares students to thrive in diverse and professional settings. Get Started Career Readiness Competencies Gain Professional Experience Internships Meet Lasell Interns Micro-Work Experiences On-Campus Jobs Explore Career Resources Major & Career Exploration Job Search Tools Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Professional Correspondence Career Outcomes Meet Our Team Discover the Path to Your Future Discover the Path to Your Future Center for Career Readiness & Internship Programs 617-243-2307 | careerdevelopment@lasell.edu Hours Monday–Friday 8:30 a.m.–4:30 p.m. Center for Career Readiness & Internship Programs 617-243-2307 | careerdevelopment@lasell.edu Hours Monday–Friday 8:30 a.m.–4:30 p.m. Get Started Career Readiness Competencies Gain Professional Experience Internships Meet Lasell Interns Micro-Work Experiences On-Campus Jobs Explore Career Resources Major & Career Exploration Job Search Tools Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Professional Correspondence Career Outcomes Meet Our Team 1844 Commonwealth Ave. Newton, MA 02466 617-243-2000 Holway Early Childhood Centers Lasell Village Workforce Development Employment Brennan Library Canvas Login Directions and Maps Bookstore Athletics Offices and Resources Media Information Campus Safety © Copyright 2026 Lasell University accessibility title IX privacy This website uses cookies to ensure that you have the best experience on our website. To find out more about the cookies we use, see our Privacy Policy . Understood"
